<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  saigon_test_grid.osm: the road map every app-level test runs with (TestRouting). It covers the Ho Chi Minh City
  points that the trip, live and end-to-end tests book trips at (TripSamples, the simulator's GPX routes).
  Generated once by a short script and then kept by hand; it is a plain grid, not a real street map.

      lat 10.802   1160 ── 1161 ── 1162 ── 1163
                    │       │       ║       │
                   ...     ...     ...     ...      17 rows, 0.002 deg (222 m) apart
                    │       │       ║       │
      lat 10.770   1000 ── 1001 ── 1002 ── 1003
              lng 106.696 106.698 106.700 106.702

  Node ids: 1000 + 10 * row + column (row 0 at lat 10.770, column 0 at lng 106.696).
  Ways: one per row (2000 + row, residential) and one per column (3000 + column, residential, except
  column 2 at lng 106.700, which is primary: the double line above). No oneway tags.
  Expected graph: 68 nodes, 16 * 4 + 17 * 3 = 115 street segments, 230 directed edges.

  Any point of the box lies within 157 m (half the cell diagonal) of a node, so nothing in it is NO_ROAD_NEARBY.
-->
